# Location Tracking (SR-App)

Detailed reference: `docs/steering/domain/location-tracking.md`. Coarse, consent-based, foreground
awareness — NOT continuous fleet tracking (ADR-004).

**Reality constraints (respect + communicate):** browser Geolocation API, requires permission; **no
reliable background tracking** (stops when app backgrounded/locked/closed); accuracy varies.

**Hard rules**
- **Capture only while relevant:** ping while a field agent has a job in `EN_ROUTE`/`IN_PROGRESS` AND the app is foregrounded. Not otherwise.
- **Location Ping** stores agent, job (nullable), lat, lng, accuracy, `capturedAt` (append-only samples).
- **Freshness is first-class:** Fresh ≤2 min; Aging 2–10 min; **Stale >10 min (must be marked "stale")**; No data = "location unavailable".
- **Consent required**; if denied, degrade gracefully — the app fully works without location (denial is not a blocking error).
- **Least-privilege visibility:** only DISPATCH/OWNER see agent locations; a field agent sees only their own; never exposed to customers.
- **Retention:** purge pings older than 30 days (MVP default). Purge runs via **Vercel Cron** daily — see `technical-scheduled-jobs` rule (ADR-016).
- Tracking on/off + permission grant/deny are audited (coarse); individual pings are NOT audit events.

**NEVER claim/imply:** 24/7 or background/closed-app tracking; real-time/continuous location; that a stale ping is current.

**DoD:** pings captured only during active foregrounded jobs w/ consent; stored with accuracy+timestamp; displayed with correct fresh/aging/stale/no-data labels; admin/owner(+self) only; retention respected; copy never overclaims.
